        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Deltana FPG42, Heavy Duty Solid Brass 42\" Offset Surface Bolt</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThis Deltana Long 42 Inch Offset Surface Door Bolt is made of solid brass and available in 9 great finishes. It can be installed horizontally or vertically on the surface of almost any door. The guides on this heavy duty door bolt are held in place with a unique ball bearing system that eliminates scratches on the barrel of the bolt, hold tension on the bolt and prevents rattling of the guides. Package includes 42 inch surface bolt, mortise strike plate, universal strike plate, angle strike plate, 3 bolt guides and matching oval phillips head finish brass wood screws.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/DEL-FPG42.gif?v=1704354642\" width=\"600\" height=\"279\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Deltana FPG42 42\" Offset Surface Bolt Specifications\">\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nAlso Available in other lengths: \r\n<a href=\"/products/solid-brass-26-inch-offset-surface-bolt-deltana-fpg26\"><b>26\" Offset Surface Bolt</b></a> - \r\n<a href=\"/products/solid-brass-18-inch-offset-surface-bolt-deltana-fpg18\"><b>18\" Offset Surface Bolt</b></a> - \r\n<a href=\"/products/solid-brass-10-inch-offset-surface-bolt-deltana-fpg10\"><b>10\" Offset Surface Bolt</b></a>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> for the Deltana FPG42 42 Inch Offset Surface Bolt:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Material: Solid Brass</li>\r\n<li>Bolt Length: 42\"</li>\r\n<li>Bolt Width: 5/8\" Diameter Half Round Rod</li>\r\n<li>Bolt Offset: 5/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Guide Width: 1-1/2\"</li>\r\n<li>Guide Projection: 9/16\"</li>\r\n<li>Knob Projection:  1-3/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Knob Diameter: 1-1/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Bolt Throw: 1-1/16\"</li>\r\n<li>Rod Resistance: 109 lbs.</li>\r\n<li>Includes 3 Strike Plates</li>\r\n<li>Packaged with all mounting hardware</li>\r\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/FPG42.pdf?v=1704262229\" target=\"new\"><b>Deltana FPG42 42 Inch Surface Bolt Dimensions (PDF)</b></a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nNo matter which finish you choose for the outside, it will still be solid brass material inside.\r\n</p>",
